    "q-24662": {
      "dom_id": "step-q24662",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Solve $g(z)=0$ where $g(z)=\\frac{{z}^{2}+4}{{z}^{2}-4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor $g(z),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(z) & =\\frac{{z}^{2}+4}{{z}^{2}-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{z}^{2}+4}{(z+2)(z-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}+4=0\n$$\n\nSince ${z}^{2}+4>0$ for all $z,$ there is no real solution to $g(z)=0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
